building something internal? the directory can do two things for your app, separately or together:

1. **gate login**: only people in an entitlement can sign in.
2. **send a groups claim**: tell your app which entitlements someone has, as a list of names you pick.

either way you write no directory code. you ask the directory, and handle what comes back through normal [OIDC](<%= doc_path("oidc-guide") %>) / [OAuth](<%= doc_path("oauth-guide") %>).

<div class="banner info">
<b>your app needs to be <code>hq_official</code>.</b>
<p>community apps can't be wired to the directory. if your app is official and you want a groups claim, it also needs the <code>groups</code> scope: ask whoever can make apps official (or a program admin) to add it.</p>
</div>

### getting set up

1. **decide what access your app needs**, named after what the app does, not the org chart (see below).
2. **file an infra ticket under "Hack Club Auth (internal)"** asking for the entitlement. say which teams or people should be in it, and whether you want to wire it yourself (you'll get `expose` on it) or have it wired for you. creating entitlements and putting whole teams into them is directory-admin only.
3. **make sure your app is `hq_official`**, and has the `groups` scope if you want the claim.
4. **wire it, and handle `access_denied`.**

